# Frontend Vue / Nuxt Rules

- Follow existing Nuxt 3 conventions in each `apps/web-*` project.
- Preserve composable, component, page, and layout structure already in use.
- Respect the current RBAC/permission model; do not bypass UI guards.
- Reuse shared components from `packages/ui` and types from `packages/shared-ts`.
- Do not duplicate API clients; align with gateway-facing contracts.
- Handle loading, error, and backend-unavailable states explicitly.
- Maintain i18n via `packages/i18n` (`ru-RU`, `en-US`, `zh-CN`).
- Do not move backend or security logic into the frontend.
- Do not hardcode tenant identity; rely on authenticated session/context patterns already used in the app.
